# One line-ending policy for the whole repository: LF in the object store and
# LF in the working tree on every platform.
#
# Why this file exists: `crates/pipes-kitti/src/cam0.rs` silently drifted to
# CRLF. It was the one file restored with `git checkout` during a revert, and on
# Windows `core.autocrlf` rewrote it on the way out because no policy said
# otherwise. Every `git add` then warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" for the
# whole tree, and a text search with LF anchors stopped matching that one file.
# Without this, anyone who re-clones or checks out a file gets different bytes
# than the ones committed.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Artifacts that must never be line-ending converted.
*.png binary
*.rrd binary
